time="2026-10-29T20:05:28.669-04:00" level=info msg="Final message: \"Cc: \\\"Paulo, Joao A\\\" <Joao_Paulo@hms.harvard.edu>\\r\\nIn-Reply-To: <SA1PR07MB87300B0A18621D233CB51C1EA76E2@SA1PR07MB8730.namprd07.prod.outlook.com>\\r\\nMIME-Version: 1.0\\r\\nReferences: <CABAFTusq88=bs1-YfjBNPr5m=2GxnPTzOA07E5LusCWtwjx=mA@mail.gmail.com> <SA1PR07MB87300B0A18621D233CB51C1EA76E2@SA1PR07MB8730.namprd07.prod.outlook.com>\\r\\nSubject: Re: Linux box network access\\r\\nTo: \\\"Cobb, Peter\\\" <peter_cobb@hms.harvard.edu>\\r\\nContent-Type: multipart/mixed; boundary=\\\"051789c8a8fa3e69d8eb37d0de07727076f9853bf66725f14bc1bec13322\\\"\\r\\nContent-Disposition: inline\\r\\n\\r\\n--051789c8a8fa3e69d8eb37d0de07727076f9853bf66725f14bc1bec13322\\r\\nContent-Disposition: inline\\r\\nContent-Type: text/plain; charset=\\\"UTF-8\\\"\\r\\n\\r\\nHi Peter,\\n\\nThank you. If it's possible to make sure this is taken care of before the end of the day tomorrow (Friday), I would appreciate it. This computer is being used by multiple people in our lab, and until SSH is enabled again, it is unusable. We have some long-running jobs we need to run over the weekend.\\n\\nI don't know if this is related, but I also noticed that it can no longer mount HMS drives (e.g. research.files). We'd like to get that re-enabled too.\\n\\nThank you,\\n\\nCaleb\\n\\nOn Thu, 29 Oct 2026 14:11:44 -0400, \\\"Cobb, Peter\\\" <peter_cobb@hms.harvard.edu> said:\\n> Hi Caleb,\\n>\\n> Ok, I will ask Network folks to set current IP address as permanent Manually assigned to this computer (on your box - DHCP). I will Also ask Network folks to make this box Remotely SSH accessible for both MAC addresses supplied. I’ll create a ticket now in your name and let you know when set.\\n>\\n> Peter\\n>\\n> Peter Cobb\\n> Harvard Medical School     IT Dept.\\n> IT Manager for Research    West Quad\\n> 45 Shattuck St.  LHRRB  Rm 119\\n> Boston, MA.    02115\\n>\\n> [signature_2992111932][shield4bev]\\n>\\n> To submit a new service request, please email: itsupport_wq@hms.harvard.edu<mailto:itsupport_wq@hms.harvard.edu>\\n>\\n> On Campus:\\n> Mondays, Wednesdays & Fridays 9 – 5pm\\n> Off Campus:\\n> Tuesdays & Thursdays 9 – 5pm\\n>\\n>\\n>\\n> From: Lindgren, Caleb <clindgren@g.harvard.edu>\\n> Date: Thursday, October 29, 2026 at 2:05\\u202fPM\\n> To: Cobb, Peter <peter_cobb@hms.harvard.edu>\\n> Cc: Paulo, Joao A <Joao_Paulo@hms.harvard.edu>\\n> Subject: Linux box network access\\n>\\n> Hi Peter,\\n>\\n> We have a Linux box that used to be in SGM 528, and we just moved it\\n> to Building C room 527A. It's plugged into an Ethernet port labelled\\n> 5053-6 (the blue cord in the attached picture), but I can't ssh into\\n> the machine anymore, nor into its iDRAC console. I logged into the\\n> physical machine and got the network information below; could you give\\n> it whatever permissions it needs for normal network access?\\n>\\n> The machine says it is on 10.119.48.0/23 and got these addresses by DHCP:\\n>\\n> Host OS   10.119.48.62    MAC 14:23:f2:e8:78:70\\n> iDRAC     10.119.48.167   MAC b4:45:06:f7:5b:88\\n>\\n> If we could also reserve the current DHCP leases that would be great\\n> so they're stable long-term.\\n>\\n> Thanks!\\n>\\n> Caleb\\n>\\r\\n--051789c8a8fa3e69d8eb37d0de07727076f9853bf66725f14bc1bec13322--\\r\\n\"" pid=19898
time="2026-10-29T20:05:29.024-04:00" level=info msg="RPC> gmail.Users.Threads.Get(email=\"me\" threadID=\"1a188d69a3761925\" fields=\"messages(id,labelIds)\") => <nil> 80.929802ms" pid=19645
time="2026-10-29T20:05:29.193-04:00" level=info msg="RPC> gmail.Users.Messages.Send(email=\"me\" threadID=\"1a188d69a3761925\" msg=\"Cc: \\\"Paulo, Joao A\\\" <Joao_Paulo@hms.harvard.edu>\\r\\nIn-Reply-To: <SA1PR07MB87300B0A18621D233CB51C1EA76E2@SA1PR07MB8730.namprd07.prod.outlook.com>\\r\\nMIME-Version: 1.0\\r\\nReferences: <CABAFTusq88=bs1-YfjBNPr5m=2GxnPTzOA07E5LusCWtwjx=mA@mail.gmail.com> <SA1PR07MB87300B0A18621D233CB51C1EA76E2@SA1PR07MB8730.namprd07.prod.outlook.com>\\r\\nSubject: Re: Linux box network access\\r\\nTo: \\\"Cobb, Peter\\\" <peter_cobb@hms.harvard.edu>\\r\\nContent-Type: multipart/mixed; boundary=\\\"051789c8a8fa3e69d8eb37d0de07727076f9853bf66725f14bc1bec13322\\\"\\r\\nContent-Disposition: inline\\r\\n\\r\\n--051789c8a8fa3e69d8eb37d0de07727076f9853bf66725f14bc1bec13322\\r\\nContent-Disposition: inline\\r\\nContent-Type: text/plain; charset=\\\"UTF-8\\\"\\r\\n\\r\\nHi Peter,\\n\\nThank you. If it's possible to make sure this is taken care of before the end of the day tomorrow (Friday), I would appreciate it. This computer is being used by multiple people in our lab, and until SSH is enabled again, it is unusable. We have some long-running jobs we need to run over the weekend.\\n\\nI don't know if this is related, but I also noticed that it can no longer mount HMS drives (e.g. research.files). We'd like to get that re-enabled too.\\n\\nThank you,\\n\\nCaleb\\n\\nOn Thu, 29 Oct 2026 14:11:44 -0400, \\\"Cobb, Peter\\\" <peter_cobb@hms.harvard.edu> said:\\n> Hi Caleb,\\n>\\n> Ok, I will ask Network folks to set current IP address as permanent Manually assigned to this computer (on your box - DHCP). I will Also ask Network folks to make this box Remotely SSH accessible for both MAC addresses supplied. I’ll create a ticket now in your name and let you know when set.\\n>\\n> Peter\\n>\\n> Peter Cobb\\n> Harvard Medical School     IT Dept.\\n> IT Manager for Research    West Quad\\n> 45 Shattuck St.  LHRRB  Rm 119\\n> Boston, MA.    02115\\n>\\n> [signature_2992111932][shield4bev]\\n>\\n> To submit a new service request, please email: itsupport_wq@hms.harvard.edu<mailto:itsupport_wq@hms.harvard.edu>\\n>\\n> On Campus:\\n> Mondays, Wednesdays & Fridays 9 – 5pm\\n> Off Campus:\\n> Tuesdays & Thursdays 9 – 5pm\\n>\\n>\\n>\\n> From: Lindgren, Caleb <clindgren@g.harvard.edu>\\n> Date: Thursday, October 29, 2026 at 2:05\\u202fPM\\n> To: Cobb, Peter <peter_cobb@hms.harvard.edu>\\n> Cc: Paulo, Joao A <Joao_Paulo@hms.harvard.edu>\\n> Subject: Linux box network access\\n>\\n> Hi Peter,\\n>\\n> We have a Linux box that used to be in SGM 528, and we just moved it\\n> to Building C room 527A. It's plugged into an Ethernet port labelled\\n> 5053-6 (the blue cord in the attached picture), but I can't ssh into\\n> the machine anymore, nor into its iDRAC console. I logged into the\\n> physical machine and got the network information below; could you give\\n> it whatever permissions it needs for normal network access?\\n>\\n> The machine says it is on 10.119.48.0/23 and got these addresses by DHCP:\\n>\\n> Host OS   10.119.48.62    MAC 14:23:f2:e8:78:70\\n> iDRAC     10.119.48.167   MAC b4:45:06:f7:5b:88\\n>\\n> If we could also reserve the current DHCP leases that would be great\\n> so they're stable long-term.\\n>\\n> Thanks!\\n>\\n> Caleb\\n>\\r\\n--051789c8a8fa3e69d8eb37d0de07727076f9853bf66725f14bc1bec13322--\\r\\n\") => <nil> 523.876289ms" pid=19898
