time="2026-11-02T09:02:05.101-05:00" level=info msg="Final message: \"Cc: \\\"Joao Paulo\\\" <Joao_Paulo@hms.harvard.edu>\\r\\nMIME-Version: 1.0\\r\\nSubject: DIA/Site quant in TMT viewer\\r\\nTo: \\\"Gygi, Steven P.\\\" <steven_gygi@hms.harvard.edu>\\r\\nContent-Type: multipart/mixed; boundary=\\\"c1a5fac9cd5967b44a47beabedeb6723c95441c103dd8f2504cfa6fc3704\\\"\\r\\nContent-Disposition: inline\\r\\n\\r\\n--c1a5fac9cd5967b44a47beabedeb6723c95441c103dd8f2504cfa6fc3704\\r\\nContent-Disposition: inline\\r\\nContent-Type: text/plain; charset=\\\"UTF-8\\\"\\r\\n\\r\\nHey guys,\\n\\nI'm not coming into lab today, but if you send me some example files I do the TMT viewer thing you were talking about. If I remember correctly, the problem is that the current DIA upload script only works with protein data, but you need it to work with peptide data so SiteQuant can use it? Also, I don't have a copy of JP's DIA converter script, so if you could send that along too that would be great.\\n\\nI'll be in tomorrow.\\n\\nCaleb\\n\\r\\n--c1a5fac9cd5967b44a47beabedeb6723c95441c103dd8f2504cfa6fc3704--\\r\\n\"" pid=7168
time="2026-11-02T09:02:06.226-05:00" level=info msg="RPC> gmail.Users.Messages.Send(email=\"me\" threadID=\"\" msg=\"Cc: \\\"Joao Paulo\\\" <Joao_Paulo@hms.harvard.edu>\\r\\nMIME-Version: 1.0\\r\\nSubject: DIA/Site quant in TMT viewer\\r\\nTo: \\\"Gygi, Steven P.\\\" <steven_gygi@hms.harvard.edu>\\r\\nContent-Type: multipart/mixed; boundary=\\\"c1a5fac9cd5967b44a47beabedeb6723c95441c103dd8f2504cfa6fc3704\\\"\\r\\nContent-Disposition: inline\\r\\n\\r\\n--c1a5fac9cd5967b44a47beabedeb6723c95441c103dd8f2504cfa6fc3704\\r\\nContent-Disposition: inline\\r\\nContent-Type: text/plain; charset=\\\"UTF-8\\\"\\r\\n\\r\\nHey guys,\\n\\nI'm not coming into lab today, but if you send me some example files I do the TMT viewer thing you were talking about. If I remember correctly, the problem is that the current DIA upload script only works with protein data, but you need it to work with peptide data so SiteQuant can use it? Also, I don't have a copy of JP's DIA converter script, so if you could send that along too that would be great.\\n\\nI'll be in tomorrow.\\n\\nCaleb\\n\\r\\n--c1a5fac9cd5967b44a47beabedeb6723c95441c103dd8f2504cfa6fc3704--\\r\\n\") => <nil> 1.125486096s" pid=7168
