time="2026-11-02T09:10:04.498-05:00" level=info msg="Final message: \"Cc: \\\"Gygi, Steven\\\" <steven_gygi@hms.harvard.edu>\\r\\nIn-Reply-To: <BL0PR07MB561755F6A62DEAC0465A7E7CB16A2@BL0PR07MB5617.namprd07.prod.outlook.com>\\r\\nMIME-Version: 1.0\\r\\nReferences: <CABAFTutzuK4So+TrzzdwyLuXeFgFn6qfZ8Y2-59m78n6R4RZgg@mail.gmail.com> <BL0PR07MB561755F6A62DEAC0465A7E7CB16A2@BL0PR07MB5617.namprd07.prod.outlook.com>\\r\\nSubject: Re: DIA/Site quant in TMT viewer\\r\\nTo: \\\"Paulo, Joao A\\\" <joao_paulo@hms.harvard.edu>\\r\\nContent-Type: multipart/mixed; boundary=\\\"4f6083dad660ed0c09f1b9dfa82b664f6cf568745398021bc1c8d255a670\\\"\\r\\nContent-Disposition: inline\\r\\n\\r\\n--4f6083dad660ed0c09f1b9dfa82b664f6cf568745398021bc1c8d255a670\\r\\nContent-Disposition: inline\\r\\nContent-Type: text/plain; charset=\\\"UTF-8\\\"\\r\\n\\r\\nOkay sounds good!\\n\\nOn Mon, 2 Nov 2026 09:03:54 -0500, \\\"Paulo, Joao A\\\" <joao_paulo@hms.harvard.edu> said:\\n> Thanks Caleb, but I set it up for Siwen over the weekend.  She says it looks correct now.\\n>\\n> ________________________________\\n> From: Lindgren, Caleb <clindgren@g.harvard.edu>\\n> Sent: Monday, November 2, 2026 9:02 AM\\n> To: Gygi, Steven <steven_gygi@hms.harvard.edu>\\n> Cc: Paulo, Joao A <Joao_Paulo@hms.harvard.edu>\\n> Subject: DIA/Site quant in TMT viewer\\n>\\n> Hey guys,\\n>\\n> I'm not coming into lab today, but if you send me some example files I\\n> do the TMT viewer thing you were talking about. If I remember\\n> correctly, the problem is that the current DIA upload script only\\n> works with protein data, but you need it to work with peptide data so\\n> SiteQuant can use it? Also, I don't have a copy of JP's DIA converter\\n> script, so if you could send that along too that would be great.\\n>\\n> I'll be in tomorrow.\\n>\\n> Caleb\\n>\\r\\n--4f6083dad660ed0c09f1b9dfa82b664f6cf568745398021bc1c8d255a670--\\r\\n\"" pid=20669
time="2026-11-02T09:10:05.236-05:00" level=info msg="RPC> gmail.Users.Messages.Send(email=\"me\" threadID=\"1a19c913a155d002\" msg=\"Cc: \\\"Gygi, Steven\\\" <steven_gygi@hms.harvard.edu>\\r\\nIn-Reply-To: <BL0PR07MB561755F6A62DEAC0465A7E7CB16A2@BL0PR07MB5617.namprd07.prod.outlook.com>\\r\\nMIME-Version: 1.0\\r\\nReferences: <CABAFTutzuK4So+TrzzdwyLuXeFgFn6qfZ8Y2-59m78n6R4RZgg@mail.gmail.com> <BL0PR07MB561755F6A62DEAC0465A7E7CB16A2@BL0PR07MB5617.namprd07.prod.outlook.com>\\r\\nSubject: Re: DIA/Site quant in TMT viewer\\r\\nTo: \\\"Paulo, Joao A\\\" <joao_paulo@hms.harvard.edu>\\r\\nContent-Type: multipart/mixed; boundary=\\\"4f6083dad660ed0c09f1b9dfa82b664f6cf568745398021bc1c8d255a670\\\"\\r\\nContent-Disposition: inline\\r\\n\\r\\n--4f6083dad660ed0c09f1b9dfa82b664f6cf568745398021bc1c8d255a670\\r\\nContent-Disposition: inline\\r\\nContent-Type: text/plain; charset=\\\"UTF-8\\\"\\r\\n\\r\\nOkay sounds good!\\n\\nOn Mon, 2 Nov 2026 09:03:54 -0500, \\\"Paulo, Joao A\\\" <joao_paulo@hms.harvard.edu> said:\\n> Thanks Caleb, but I set it up for Siwen over the weekend.  She says it looks correct now.\\n>\\n> ________________________________\\n> From: Lindgren, Caleb <clindgren@g.harvard.edu>\\n> Sent: Monday, November 2, 2026 9:02 AM\\n> To: Gygi, Steven <steven_gygi@hms.harvard.edu>\\n> Cc: Paulo, Joao A <Joao_Paulo@hms.harvard.edu>\\n> Subject: DIA/Site quant in TMT viewer\\n>\\n> Hey guys,\\n>\\n> I'm not coming into lab today, but if you send me some example files I\\n> do the TMT viewer thing you were talking about. If I remember\\n> correctly, the problem is that the current DIA upload script only\\n> works with protein data, but you need it to work with peptide data so\\n> SiteQuant can use it? Also, I don't have a copy of JP's DIA converter\\n> script, so if you could send that along too that would be great.\\n>\\n> I'll be in tomorrow.\\n>\\n> Caleb\\n>\\r\\n--4f6083dad660ed0c09f1b9dfa82b664f6cf568745398021bc1c8d255a670--\\r\\n\") => <nil> 738.219886ms" pid=20669
