time="2026-11-02T14:00:37.953-05:00" level=info msg="Final message: \"In-Reply-To: <SA1PR07MB8730D1EEE04CA70E0488D611A76C2@SA1PR07MB8730.namprd07.prod.outlook.com>\\r\\nMIME-Version: 1.0\\r\\nReferences: <CABAFTusq88=bs1-YfjBNPr5m=2GxnPTzOA07E5LusCWtwjx=mA@mail.gmail.com> <SA1PR07MB87300B0A18621D233CB51C1EA76E2@SA1PR07MB8730.namprd07.prod.outlook.com> <CABAFTuvt1uL+XKUQoU0zkYNMfhMJGXXMwyGyr-e_1KSLkucoVQ@mail.gmail.com> <SA1PR07MB8730CDC5D8C63E66A8FA68A8A76D2@SA1PR07MB8730.namprd07.prod.outlook.com> <9BF27A57-465C-464C-BE2A-BD530D0D9745@hms.harvard.edu> <CABAFTusB8ppnETUWU+vde=dKY6R4dscCqoujdd8KQbMBWA71hw@mail.gmail.com> <SA1PR07MB8730D1EEE04CA70E0488D611A76C2@SA1PR07MB8730.namprd07.prod.outlook.com>\\r\\nSubject: Re: Linux box network access\\r\\nTo: \\\"Cobb, Peter\\\" <peter_cobb@hms.harvard.edu>\\r\\nContent-Type: multipart/mixed; boundary=\\\"8e626f885b1a5d79153681194ce2313820bd2d7907003a6fe9fb171739c4\\\"\\r\\nContent-Disposition: inline\\r\\n\\r\\n--8e626f885b1a5d79153681194ce2313820bd2d7907003a6fe9fb171739c4\\r\\nContent-Disposition: inline\\r\\nContent-Type: text/plain; charset=\\\"UTF-8\\\"\\r\\n\\r\\nHi Peter,\\n\\nHope your Monday is going well. Just wanted to check how it went with the network people this morning?\\n\\nThanks,\\n\\nCaleb\\n\\nOn Sat, 31 Oct 2026 10:17:54 -0400, \\\"Cobb, Peter\\\" <peter_cobb@hms.harvard.edu> said:\\n> Hi Caleb,\\n>\\n> My apologies on this not working yet. I’ll ping Network folks again to have them look into this again Monday morning to get this working.\\n>\\n> Peter\\n>\\n> Peter Cobb\\n> Harvard Medical School     IT Dept.\\n> IT Manager for Research    West Quad\\n> 45 Shattuck St.  LHRRB  Rm 119\\n> Boston, MA.    02115\\n>\\n> [signature_2992111932][shield4bev]\\n>\\n> To submit a new service request, please email: itsupport_wq@hms.harvard.edu<mailto:itsupport_wq@hms.harvard.edu>\\n>\\n> On Campus:\\n> Mondays, Wednesdays & Fridays 9 – 5pm\\n> Off Campus:\\n> Tuesdays & Thursdays 9 – 5pm\\n>\\n>\\n>\\n> From: Lindgren, Caleb <clindgren@g.harvard.edu>\\n> Date: Friday, October 30, 2026 at 5:32\\u202fPM\\n> To: Cobb, Peter <peter_cobb@hms.harvard.edu>\\n> Cc: Paulo, Joao A <joao_paulo@hms.harvard.edu>\\n> Subject: Re: Linux box network access\\n>\\n> Hi Peter,\\n>\\n> Thank you for your help. I rebooted the computer, but unfortunately\\n> it's still not working. When I try to ssh in to either IP address, I'm\\n> still getting the same error as before, e.g. \\\"ssh: connect to host\\n> 10.119.48.62 port 22: Connection timed out\\\"\\n>\\n> Additionally, when I try to mount research.files, I get \\\"CIFS: VFS:\\n> Error connecting to socket. Aborting operation.\\\"\\n>\\n> Let me know if there's any more information you need from me. Thanks\\n> again for trying to expedite this, no worries that we didn't get it\\n> working before the weekend, we'll manage.\\n>\\n> Thanks,\\n>\\n> Caleb\\n>\\n> On Fri, 30 Oct 2026 16:39:02 -0400, \\\"Cobb, Peter\\\"\\n> <peter_cobb@hms.harvard.edu> said:\\n>>\\n>> Hi Caleb,\\n>>\\n>> Although you may need to Reboot computer, this request should be all set now. Please feel free to try this out now. Thanks!\\n>>\\n>> Peter\\n>>\\n>> On Oct 30, 2026, at 9:50\\u202fAM, Cobb, Peter <peter_cobb@hms.harvard.edu> wrote:\\n>>\\n>> \\ufeff\\n>> Hi Caleb,\\n>>\\n>> We’ll do our best to get this set today. I just pinged Network folks to ask them this though. I’ll let you know when they say it’s set.\\n>>\\n>> Peter\\n>>\\n>> Peter Cobb\\n>> Harvard Medical School     IT Dept.\\n>> IT Manager for Research    West Quad\\n>> 45 Shattuck St.  LHRRB  Rm 119\\n>> Boston, MA.    02115\\n>>\\n>> [image001.png][image002.png]\\n>>\\n>> To submit a new service request, please email: itsupport_wq@hms.harvard.edu<mailto:itsupport_wq@hms.harvard.edu>\\n>>\\n>> On Campus:\\n>> Mondays, Wednesdays & Fridays 9 – 5pm\\n>> Off Campus:\\n>> Tuesdays & Thursdays 9 – 5pm\\n>>\\n>>\\n>>\\n>> From: Lindgren, Caleb <clindgren@g.harvard.edu>\\n>> Date: Thursday, October 29, 2026 at 8:05\\u202fPM\\n>> To: Cobb, Peter <peter_cobb@hms.harvard.edu>\\n>> Cc: Paulo, Joao A <Joao_Paulo@hms.harvard.edu>\\n>> Subject: Re: Linux box network access\\n>>\\n>> Hi Peter,\\n>>\\n>> Thank you. If it's possible to make sure this is taken care of before\\n>> the end of the day tomorrow (Friday), I would appreciate it. This\\n>> computer is being used by multiple people in our lab, and until SSH is\\n>> enabled again, it is unusable. We have some long-running jobs we need\\n>> to run over the weekend.\\n>>\\n>> I don't know if this is related, but I also noticed that it can no\\n>> longer mount HMS drives (e.g. research.files). We'd like to get that\\n>> re-enabled too.\\n>>\\n>> Thank you,\\n>>\\n>> Caleb\\n>>\\n>> On Thu, 29 Oct 2026 14:11:44 -0400, \\\"Cobb, Peter\\\"\\n>> <peter_cobb@hms.harvard.edu> said:\\n>>> Hi Caleb,\\n>>>\\n>>> Ok, I will ask Network folks to set current IP address as permanent Manually assigned to this computer (on your box - DHCP). I will Also ask Network folks to make this box Remotely SSH accessible for both MAC addresses supplied. I’ll create a ticket now in your name and let you know when set.\\n>>>\\n>>> Peter\\n>>>\\n>>> Peter Cobb\\n>>> Harvard Medical School     IT Dept.\\n>>> IT Manager for Research    West Quad\\n>>> 45 Shattuck St.  LHRRB  Rm 119\\n>>> Boston, MA.    02115\\n>>>\\n>>> [signature_2992111932][shield4bev]\\n>>>\\n>>> To submit a new service request, please email: itsupport_wq@hms.harvard.edu<mailto:itsupport_wq@hms.harvard.edu>\\n>>>\\n>>> On Campus:\\n>>> Mondays, Wednesdays & Fridays 9 – 5pm\\n>>> Off Campus:\\n>>> Tuesdays & Thursdays 9 – 5pm\\n>>>\\n>>>\\n>>>\\n>>> From: Lindgren, Caleb <clindgren@g.harvard.edu>\\n>>> Date: Thursday, October 29, 2026 at 2:05\\u202fPM\\n>>> To: Cobb, Peter <peter_cobb@hms.harvard.edu>\\n>>> Cc: Paulo, Joao A <Joao_Paulo@hms.harvard.edu>\\n>>> Subject: Linux box network access\\n>>>\\n>>> Hi Peter,\\n>>>\\n>>> We have a Linux box that used to be in SGM 528, and we just moved it\\n>>> to Building C room 527A. It's plugged into an Ethernet port labelled\\n>>> 5053-6 (the blue cord in the attached picture), but I can't ssh into\\n>>> the machine anymore, nor into its iDRAC console. I logged into the\\n>>> physical machine and got the network information below; could you give\\n>>> it whatever permissions it needs for normal network access?\\n>>>\\n>>> The machine says it is on 10.119.48.0/23 and got these addresses by DHCP:\\n>>>\\n>>> Host OS   10.119.48.62    MAC 14:23:f2:e8:78:70\\n>>> iDRAC     10.119.48.167   MAC b4:45:06:f7:5b:88\\n>>>\\n>>> If we could also reserve the current DHCP leases that would be great\\n>>> so they're stable long-term.\\n>>>\\n>>> Thanks!\\n>>>\\n>>> Caleb\\n>>>\\n>>\\n>\\r\\n--8e626f885b1a5d79153681194ce2313820bd2d7907003a6fe9fb171739c4--\\r\\n\"" pid=31013
time="2026-11-02T14:00:38.393-05:00" level=info msg="RPC> gmail.Users.Messages.Send(email=\"me\" threadID=\"1a188d69a3761925\" msg=\"In-Reply-To: <SA1PR07MB8730D1EEE04CA70E0488D611A76C2@SA1PR07MB8730.namprd07.prod.outlook.com>\\r\\nMIME-Version: 1.0\\r\\nReferences: <CABAFTusq88=bs1-YfjBNPr5m=2GxnPTzOA07E5LusCWtwjx=mA@mail.gmail.com> <SA1PR07MB87300B0A18621D233CB51C1EA76E2@SA1PR07MB8730.namprd07.prod.outlook.com> <CABAFTuvt1uL+XKUQoU0zkYNMfhMJGXXMwyGyr-e_1KSLkucoVQ@mail.gmail.com> <SA1PR07MB8730CDC5D8C63E66A8FA68A8A76D2@SA1PR07MB8730.namprd07.prod.outlook.com> <9BF27A57-465C-464C-BE2A-BD530D0D9745@hms.harvard.edu> <CABAFTusB8ppnETUWU+vde=dKY6R4dscCqoujdd8KQbMBWA71hw@mail.gmail.com> <SA1PR07MB8730D1EEE04CA70E0488D611A76C2@SA1PR07MB8730.namprd07.prod.outlook.com>\\r\\nSubject: Re: Linux box network access\\r\\nTo: \\\"Cobb, Peter\\\" <peter_cobb@hms.harvard.edu>\\r\\nContent-Type: multipart/mixed; boundary=\\\"8e626f885b1a5d79153681194ce2313820bd2d7907003a6fe9fb171739c4\\\"\\r\\nContent-Disposition: inline\\r\\n\\r\\n--8e626f885b1a5d79153681194ce2313820bd2d7907003a6fe9fb171739c4\\r\\nContent-Disposition: inline\\r\\nContent-Type: text/plain; charset=\\\"UTF-8\\\"\\r\\n\\r\\nHi Peter,\\n\\nHope your Monday is going well. Just wanted to check how it went with the network people this morning?\\n\\nThanks,\\n\\nCaleb\\n\\nOn Sat, 31 Oct 2026 10:17:54 -0400, \\\"Cobb, Peter\\\" <peter_cobb@hms.harvard.edu> said:\\n> Hi Caleb,\\n>\\n> My apologies on this not working yet. I’ll ping Network folks again to have them look into this again Monday morning to get this working.\\n>\\n> Peter\\n>\\n> Peter Cobb\\n> Harvard Medical School     IT Dept.\\n> IT Manager for Research    West Quad\\n> 45 Shattuck St.  LHRRB  Rm 119\\n> Boston, MA.    02115\\n>\\n> [signature_2992111932][shield4bev]\\n>\\n> To submit a new service request, please email: itsupport_wq@hms.harvard.edu<mailto:itsupport_wq@hms.harvard.edu>\\n>\\n> On Campus:\\n> Mondays, Wednesdays & Fridays 9 – 5pm\\n> Off Campus:\\n> Tuesdays & Thursdays 9 – 5pm\\n>\\n>\\n>\\n> From: Lindgren, Caleb <clindgren@g.harvard.edu>\\n> Date: Friday, October 30, 2026 at 5:32\\u202fPM\\n> To: Cobb, Peter <peter_cobb@hms.harvard.edu>\\n> Cc: Paulo, Joao A <joao_paulo@hms.harvard.edu>\\n> Subject: Re: Linux box network access\\n>\\n> Hi Peter,\\n>\\n> Thank you for your help. I rebooted the computer, but unfortunately\\n> it's still not working. When I try to ssh in to either IP address, I'm\\n> still getting the same error as before, e.g. \\\"ssh: connect to host\\n> 10.119.48.62 port 22: Connection timed out\\\"\\n>\\n> Additionally, when I try to mount research.files, I get \\\"CIFS: VFS:\\n> Error connecting to socket. Aborting operation.\\\"\\n>\\n> Let me know if there's any more information you need from me. Thanks\\n> again for trying to expedite this, no worries that we didn't get it\\n> working before the weekend, we'll manage.\\n>\\n> Thanks,\\n>\\n> Caleb\\n>\\n> On Fri, 30 Oct 2026 16:39:02 -0400, \\\"Cobb, Peter\\\"\\n> <peter_cobb@hms.harvard.edu> said:\\n>>\\n>> Hi Caleb,\\n>>\\n>> Although you may need to Reboot computer, this request should be all set now. Please feel free to try this out now. Thanks!\\n>>\\n>> Peter\\n>>\\n>> On Oct 30, 2026, at 9:50\\u202fAM, Cobb, Peter <peter_cobb@hms.harvard.edu> wrote:\\n>>\\n>> \\ufeff\\n>> Hi Caleb,\\n>>\\n>> We’ll do our best to get this set today. I just pinged Network folks to ask them this though. I’ll let you know when they say it’s set.\\n>>\\n>> Peter\\n>>\\n>> Peter Cobb\\n>> Harvard Medical School     IT Dept.\\n>> IT Manager for Research    West Quad\\n>> 45 Shattuck St.  LHRRB  Rm 119\\n>> Boston, MA.    02115\\n>>\\n>> [image001.png][image002.png]\\n>>\\n>> To submit a new service request, please email: itsupport_wq@hms.harvard.edu<mailto:itsupport_wq@hms.harvard.edu>\\n>>\\n>> On Campus:\\n>> Mondays, Wednesdays & Fridays 9 – 5pm\\n>> Off Campus:\\n>> Tuesdays & Thursdays 9 – 5pm\\n>>\\n>>\\n>>\\n>> From: Lindgren, Caleb <clin